# Under the Shadow of the Ivory Tower (Q343): a level 40 human mystic accepts at Cema; with no
# orb she asks for them; twelve gargoyles give twelve orbs (every roll pinned to succeed);
# Marsha's first talk opens her game; she takes 10 orbs, draws 10 and 1 (the second card, hint
# 08b), and the third guess wins 20; two more gargoyles each give an orb, the first lowering
# memoStateEx on a roll of 12 (at most 12), the second not on 13; Trumpin's game climbs four
# wins (05 to 05c), pays 310 on the fifth, loses 10 on a roll of 1 for 05, then wins on 07 and
# pays 10 at the first step; Icarus trades a liqueur for 401 C-grade spiritshots (rolls 200 and
# 0), the second for a scroll of escape (roll 600), then has no liqueur; Cema pays 120 an orb and
# the player gives up; then relog. Expectations replay the reference trace of this scenario.
